        "spec": {
          "id": 2,
          "title": "repeat references in the new table by network",
          "description": "The same references beyond the first, summed over all hosts and split by the network of the referenced address. Onion and i2p dominate: their addresses share only sixteen network groups each, so a node reachable over Tor or I2P keeps hearing the same addresses from many source groups. Add host to the by clause to see which node a network total comes from.",
