          "id": 3,
          "title": "references per distinct address in the new table",
          "description": "Positions divided by distinct address and port combinations: the mean number of buckets referencing one address. One means every address sits in a single bucket. It says the same thing as the panel above without the table size, which makes nodes comparable; read the two together, because a ratio of 1.15 on a full table is ten thousand positions.",
